# Laravel Eloquent Relationships & Pivot Tables

## Complete Step-by-Step Practical Guide

This guide builds the following Laravel structure from scratch:

```text
Department
    │
    │ hasMany
    ▼
Employee
    │
    │ belongsToMany
    ▼
employee_project
    │
    │ belongsToMany
    ▼
Project
```

We will learn:

* One-to-many relationships
* Many-to-many relationships
* Pivot tables
* `belongsToMany()`
* `withPivot()`
* `withTimestamps()`
* `attach()`
* `detach()`
* `updateExistingPivot()`
* `sync()`
* `syncWithoutDetaching()`
* `wherePivot()`
* `wherePivotIn()`
* `wherePivotNull()`
* `wherePivotNotNull()`
* `orderByPivot()`
* `with()`
* `load()`
* Local scopes
* Laravel naming conventions
* Custom pivot table names
* Custom foreign keys
* How all the tables and models connect together

---

# 1. What We Are Building

We will create four database tables:

```text
departments
employees
projects
employee_project
```

The important point is:

```text
departments
    ↓
employees
```

is a **one-to-many** relationship.

One department can have many employees.

Then:

```text
employees
    ↓
employee_project
    ↓
projects
```

is a **many-to-many** relationship.

One employee can work on many projects.

One project can have many employees.

The `employee_project` table is called a **pivot table**.

