# 9. Understanding cascadeOnDelete()

This:

```php
->cascadeOnDelete();
```

means:

If a department is deleted, its employees will also be deleted.

Example:

```text
Department IT
    ↓
John
Sarah
```

If IT is deleted:

```text
IT
John
Sarah
```

will be deleted.

Use this carefully because deleting a parent can delete related records.

