# 18. Understanding belongsTo()

This:

```php
public function department(): BelongsTo
{
    return $this->belongsTo(Department::class);
}
```

means:

```text
Employee
   ↓
belongs to
   ↓
Department
```

The employee has:

```text
department_id
```

Laravel uses that foreign key to find the department.

For example:

```text
employees

id | department_id | name
---|---------------|------
1  | 2             | John
```

Laravel looks at:

```text
department_id = 2
```

and finds:

```text
departments

id | name
---|------
2  | IT
```

So:

```php
$employee->department;
```

returns:

```text
IT
```

