# 25. attach()

`attach()` creates a relationship in the pivot table.

For example:

```php
$john->projects()->attach($project1->id, [
    'role' => 'developer',
]);
```

This creates approximately:

```text
employee_project

employee_id | project_id | role
------------|------------|----------
1           | 1          | developer
```

You can attach another project:

```php
$john->projects()->attach($project2->id, [
    'role' => 'tester',
]);
```

Now:

```text
employee_id | project_id | role
------------|------------|----------
1           | 1          | developer
1           | 2          | tester
```

---

# 26. attach() With Multiple Projects

You can attach multiple projects:

```php
$john->projects()->attach([
    $project1->id => [
        'role' => 'developer',
    ],

    $project2->id => [
        'role' => 'tester',
    ],
]);
```

Result:

```text
employee_id | project_id | role
------------|------------|----------
1           | 1          | developer
1           | 2          | tester
```

