# 41. Adding More Pivot Columns

Currently we have:

```text
employee_project

employee_id
project_id
role
created_at
updated_at
```

Suppose we want:

```text
assigned_at
completed_at
hours_per_week
```

Then migration could contain:

```php
Schema::create('employee_project', function (Blueprint $table) {
    $table->id();

    $table->foreignId('employee_id')
          ->constrained('employees')
          ->cascadeOnDelete();

    $table->foreignId('project_id')
          ->constrained('projects')
          ->cascadeOnDelete();

    $table->string('role');

    $table->date('assigned_at')->nullable();

    $table->timestamp('completed_at')->nullable();

    $table->integer('hours_per_week')->nullable();

    $table->timestamps();
});
```

Then expose them:

```php
public function projects(): BelongsToMany
{
    return $this->belongsToMany(Project::class)
                ->withPivot([
                    'role',
                    'assigned_at',
                    'completed_at',
                    'hours_per_week',
                ])
                ->withTimestamps();
}
```

Then:

```php
$project->pivot->role;

$project->pivot->assigned_at;

$project->pivot->completed_at;

$project->pivot->hours_per_week;
```

