# 71. Complete Practical Example

After creating the models and migrations:

```bash
php artisan migrate
```

Then:

```bash
php artisan tinker
```

Create a department:

```php
$it = Department::create([
    'name' => 'IT',
    'description' => 'Information Technology',
]);
```

Create an employee:

```php
$john = Employee::create([
    'department_id' => $it->id,
    'name' => 'John',
    'email' => 'john@example.com',
    'joining_date' => '2025-01-10',
    'is_active' => true,
    'salary' => 50000,
]);
```

Create a project:

```php
$project = Project::create([
    'name' => 'E-commerce Website',
    'description' => 'Online shopping platform',
]);
```

Assign John to the project:

```php
$john->projects()->attach($project->id, [
    'role' => 'developer',
]);
```

Now the database looks like:

```text
departments

id | name
---|-----
1  | IT
```

```text
employees

id | department_id | name
---|---------------|------
1  | 1             | John
```

```text
projects

id | name
---|------------------
1  | E-commerce Website
```

```text
employee_project

employee_id | project_id | role
------------|------------|----------
1           | 1          | developer
```

Now:

```php
$john->projects;
```

returns John's projects.

And:

```php
$john->projects->first()->pivot->role;
```

returns:

```text
developer
```

